// The bottomless compost bucket.
//
// A bucket of compost poured in is worth TWO uses, which is the whole point of the item - OSRS
// doubles a bucket rather than just carrying it. 10,000 uses in total, and 5,000 buckets accepted
// in one Fill, both OSRS's own numbers.
^compost_bucket_max = 10000
^compost_bucket_per_bucket = 2
^compost_bucket_fill_max = 5000

// WHERE IT COMES FROM. OSRS drops it from the Hespori, a 2019 Farming Guild boss with no content
// here, so it is found while farming instead - a Farming reward for Farming, which is the part of
// the OSRS source that matters. The roll rides ~farming_xp, the one chokepoint every Farming award
// already goes through, and succeeds with probability xp/^bottomless_roll_xp: proportional to what
// the action was worth, so a magic tree pays for the hours it took and raking a patch does not.
//
// 120,000 is deliberately steeper than a skilling outfit piece at 50,000. There is exactly one of
// these to find, it never needs replacing, and it is the only compost bucket you will ever want -
// so it should be a thing you remember getting, not the fourth item of a set.
^bottomless_roll_xp = 120000

// And not before 60 Farming. Compost matters least at the levels where you are planting allotments
// you could replace for nothing; the gate is there so the reward lands when the work it saves is
// real, and so a brand-new character does not open Farming by finding the endgame bucket.
^bottomless_roll_level = 60

